hevc-rs
Copyright 2026 Chris Dobbyn

hevc-rs is a new crate, not a port of a Go repository. It implements ITU-T Recommendation
H.265 (High efficiency video coding). The tables in the source (CABAC context initialisation
values, rangeTabLps, intra angles, the transform matrix, default scaling lists, the deblocking
beta/tC tables, the chroma QP table) come from that Recommendation.

libde265 (LGPL-3.0) and FFmpeg (LGPL-2.1) are used only as CI-only oracle tools and as design
references. No code or tables are copied from them.

Third-party code and data
-------------------------

1. MD5 (src/sei.rs) is written from RFC 1321 (R. Rivest, 1992), which places the algorithm
   description in the public domain for any use.

2. JCT-VC HEVC conformance bitstreams (ITU-T H.265.1), used only in CI as parity inputs; they
   are downloaded at build time and never committed.
